\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2010\par 03:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates Philippine measures)\par \par \uc2 Nov 5 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening as investors, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies, pour money into higher-yielding markets.\par \par \uc2 Below are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA WANTS WEAKER RAND, ADMITS IT WILL BE DIFFICULT\par \par \uc2 * New long-term growth plan envisages "a careful balancing of more active monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve growth...through a more competitive exchange rate and a lower cost of capital," government says on Oct. 26.\par \par \uc2 * Government insists this does not violate G20 agreement, to which South Africa subscribed three days earlier, to avoid competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations.\par \par \uc2 * Government says it will build up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to curb rand <ZAR=> appreciation.\par \par \uc2 * But analysts doubt it has financial muscle to force down rand; finance minister says international cooperation needed.\par \par \uc2 * Treasury Director General says tax on capital inflows into bond market would not work for South Africa.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE69Q1Q1] [ID:nLDE69P111]\par \par \uc2 TURKEY STEPS UP \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\uc2  BUYING\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says on Oct. 1 it will raise the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it buys at weekly auctions, as the lira <TRY=> hits its strongest versus the dollar in almost a year.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official says it will buy a maximum of $500 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  each week; previously, it usually bought $200 million with an option of buying a further $200 million.\par \par \uc2 * Prime minister recently said Turkey needed to build up its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nLDE6901OR]\par \par \uc2 THAILAND TAXES FOREIGN BOND INVESTORS\par \par \uc2 * Thailand imposes 15 pct withholding tax on interest and capital gains earned by foreign investors on Thai bonds.\par \par \uc2 * Tax became effective Oct. 13, 2010, applicable to bonds issued by government, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state enterprises.\par \par \uc2 * The baht <THB=> has risen about 11 percent against the U.S. dollar this year to levels not seen since the 1997 Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nSGE69K03E] [ID:nSGE69B0A6]\par \par \uc2 JAPAN CUTS RATES, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME SINCE 2004\par \par \uc2 * Bank of Japan unexpectedly pledged to pump more funds into the economy on Oct. 5 and launched "comprehensive monetary easing," cutting interest rates to virtually zero.\par \par \uc2 * Authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15, the first time since 2004, to drive down the yen <JPY=>, selling an estimated 2 trillion yen. Figures later showed September sales totalled 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.4 billion).\par \par \uc2 * Prime minister signals Tokyo to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says United States did not comment on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at meeting in Washington on Oct. 9.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nTOE69801I]\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL TAKES MORE AGGRESSIVE ACTION\par \par \uc2 * Brazil warns of "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war."\par \par \uc2 * Government raises tax on foreigners buying local bonds for second time since start of October.\par \par \uc2 * Also raises derivatives tax.\par \par \uc2 * Brazil sovereign fund yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up daily dollar auctions <BRL=>.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nN18280200]\par \par \uc2 CHILE ALLOWS PENSION FUNDS TO HOLD MORE ASSETS ABROAD\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifts limits on pension funds' overseas investment.\par \par \uc2 * Chilean President Sebastian Pinera says worried by strong peso but no plans for capital controls.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slows pace of rate hikes, citing peso <CLP=>.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief says weighing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Government to cut red tape to help exporters hit by peso.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nN04221079] [ID:nN20242719]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA WARNS OF NEW LIMITS\par \par \uc2 * Regulator warns of further measures on forwards, asks banks not to lend in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says will take new steps if foreign debt grows too fast.\par \par \uc2 * Authorities repeatedly spotted buying dollars to curb the pace of appreciation in the won <KRW=>.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose more than $4 billion in September to a record level of $290 billion.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nTOE69401M] [ID:nTOE697020] [ID:nTOE690069] [ID:nTOE69H00M]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 * Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars <INR=> for the first time this year, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nSGE69D0EX]\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINES RELAXES \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RULES IN RESPONSE TO INFLOWS\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  approved in late October six measures, involving higher ceilings for residents' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases and outward investments, and encouraging foreign debt prepayments by the private sector -- moves aimed at encouraging outflows of capital and dampening a peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PHP=PDSP> that has reached 2-year highs.\par \par \uc2 * Bank to stay active in market as peso <PHP=> rises.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nSGE69R0EK] [ID:nSGE69R0I4]\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WIDENS RANGE OF MATURITIES\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says expects stable rupiah <IDR=>.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says unworried about capital inflows, will try to manage rupiah.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a minimum holding period for its bills in June by offering a wider range of maturities.\par \par \uc2 * Investors must hold the bills for minimum of one month.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nJAK423860] [ID:nJAK536689] [ID:nSGE65F0BV] [ID:nWAT014685]\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA PLANS DOLLAR PURCHASES, CUTS DOLLAR INFLOW\par \par \uc2 * Up to $3.7 bln forwards market purchases in 2011\par \par \uc2 * Govt will not bring in $1.5 bln this year, 2011\par \par \uc2 * Eliminates tax exemption on foreign loan interest\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying at least $20 million daily.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nN29291838]\par \par \uc2 PERU PLANS TO LIMIT \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  FORWARDS, EASES FUND OUTFLOWS\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank orders new rise in minimum deposit requirements.\par \par \uc2 * Banking regulator eyes limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards.\par \par \uc2 * Rates on hold, possibly easing pressure on sol <PEN=>.\par \par \uc2 * Pension funds allowed to hold more assets abroad.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading near two-year high against dollar.\par \par \uc2 * Peru's sol boosted by 6-7 pct growth in 2011.\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nN21106328]\par \par \uc2 MEXICO SAYS NO PLANS FOR CAPITAL CONTROLS\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says restrictions won't work. <MXN=>\par \par \uc2 -- Story link: [ID:nWBT014190]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CONTROLS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101108e6b500028\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
