\par\par \b \uc2 FUND VIEW-Aviva favours won, rupee among emerging  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 11:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 19 (Reuters) - Good yield differentials and a low likelihood of stringent capital controls make the Korean won and Indian rupee among the best emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bets against a weak dollar, a fund manager at Aviva said.\par \par \uc2  Kieran Curtis, who helps manage $1.4 billion in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerging debt at UK insurer Aviva, says that based on real effective exchange rate (REER) analysis, the Korean won <KRW=>, the Philippine peso <PHP=> and the Indian rupee <INR=> look the most attractively valued Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  In Latin America, the Mexican peso <MXN=> stands out and in emerging Europe, the Polish zloty <PLN=> and Hungarian forint <HUF=> could have some upside, says Curtis, whose fund gets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure via local emerging debt and also uses forwards as an overlay to optimise \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  returns.\par \par \uc2  "Basically, positioning and pressure on valuations on these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weaker than, say, on the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> and Brazilian real <BRL=>," he said. "In theory they have more room to appreciate than most other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2  Expectation of additional large doses of monetary stimulus for the U.S. economy has kicked the dollar to multi-year lows against many emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fuelling fears more developing countries will bring in measures to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2  Brazil on Monday raised its levy on bond inflows to 6 percent while Thailand has put a 15 percent tax on interest and capital gains on Thai bonds. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's finance minister said on Tuesday the government is preparing measures to deal with problems caused by foreign capital flows, while \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in rupee markets last week for the first time this year.\par \par \uc2  But Curtis said investors must learn to deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls or seek out markets where curbs may be less punitive.\par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Korea is active but has never really been successful in controlling the strength or volatility of the won," Curtis said.\par \par \uc2  "Inflation in Asia is more stable and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  still look cheap on (an) absolute basis," he said. "They are not places that really manipulate their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  much."\par \par \uc2  TURKISH BONDS OVERVALUED\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation and the collapse in core yields have pushed year-to-date returns on emerging local bonds <.JGEGDCM> to around 17 percent.\par \par \uc2  Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should benefit if the German economy continues to improve, Curtis says though he remains underweight the forint <EURHUF=>, citing uncertainty over Hungary's ability to tackle its budget deficit and its relationship with the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2  Unlike the Fed and Bank of Japan, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not embarked on more stimulus, pushing the euro <EUR=> to a recent eight-month high against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The risk for the forint and zloty is that they could get a kick from any ECB policy change. But the eurozone can tolerate \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength in the short term and that is good for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that trade high-beta to the euro," Curtis added.\par \par \uc2  Curtis is neutral on the Brazilian real, noting that the rise in the inflows tax will affect future flows.\par \par \uc2  "You have to be a medium or long-term investor to make it worthwhile ... You have to hold (the bonds) for over a year to realise the value," he said. \par \par \uc2  Curtis acknowleges signs of overvaluation in some emerging local bond curves. He cites Turkey where interest rates are 7 percent despite five-year average inflation at 8.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  "In many countries interest rates ought to be higher and bond curves ought to be a bit higher. They look a bit expensive. But they are still very inexpensive compared with core markets."  (Editing by Susan Fenton)     \par \par \uc2 EMERGING-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FUND VIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|HX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101022e6aj000r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
