\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee snaps 3-day gains as euro slips\b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2010\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro's losses versus dollar weigh on rupee sentiment\par \par \uc2 * Early losses in local shares also hurt the local unit\par \par \uc2 * Rupee to underperform Asian peers in medium term: BarCap\par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen at 42/dollar by mid-2011: DBS (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Swati Bhat\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee on Monday snapped a three-day winning streak as the dollar's gains versus major units overseas weighed, but hopes for capital inflows stayed firm with the launch of the country's largest-ever share sale.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> closed at 44.36/37 per dollar, 0.6 percent below 44.10/11 at close on Friday, when the rupee rose as high as 43.95, its highest since Aug. 29, 2008. The rupee traded in a band of 44.1800-44.4150 during the day.\par \par \uc2 "I was anticipating today's move. Euro also started reversal from $1.4100 and stocks also seem to be heading lower. After the mega flows, there should be some reversal," said Hari Chandramgathan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Federal Bank.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar bounced from a 10-month low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, as investors uncertain about the extent of monetary easing by the Federal Reserve trimmed bearish bets against the greenback. [USD/]\par \par \uc2 The index of the dollar <.DXY> against six majors was down 0.4 percent when the rupee market closed.\par \par \uc2 "We think room for further appreciation of the INR is limited, as short USD positions are showing signs of being overstretched and the RBI is likely to join other Asian central banks in trying to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation," analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  wrote in a daily note.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Duvvuri Subbarao said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if inflows turn lumpy. [ID:nSGE69E0CM]\par \par \uc2 Traders said they will continue to closely watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, which bought dollars on Thursday in a move they believe was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. [ID:nSGE69D0EX]\par \par \uc2 "It is highly likely that the \uc2 Coal India\uc2  IPO will be highly oversubscribed and we could see some FII repatriation once the IPO allocation is finalised," analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We look for USD/INR to move in a range of 43.90 to 44.50 for the week with an upside bias. In the medium term, we think the rising current account deficit and weaker fundamentals are likely to result in INR underperforming against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 The world's largest coal miner \uc2 Coal India\uc2 's $3.5 billion initial public offering is currently underway and is expected to see a flood of foreign capital inflows. [ID:nSGE68T06Y]\par \par \uc2 "Globally, USD was stronger today, so a bit of that's rubbed off on INR," said Ananth Narayan G., head of fixed income, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities, South Asia at Standard Chartered Bank in Mumbai.\par \par \uc2 Early losses in local shares also hurt the rupee. Shares <.BSESN> reversed early losses and eked out a 0.2 percent gain on Monday, as robust foreign fund interest and strong September quarter earnings overshadowed the pressure from the launch of country's biggest-ever initial share offer. [.BO]\par \par \uc2 For the year to date, the rupee is up 4.9 percent on record $23.3 billion foreign fund inflows into shares.\par \par \uc2 "We are looking generally for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate against the dollar about 5-6 percent per year for next five years," said David W. Carbon, managing director of economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at DBS.\par \par \uc2 He said DBS expects the rupee to be at 42 to the dollar by mid-2011.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts <PNDF> were quoted at 44.73, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market <INRFUTURES>, the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, MCX-SX and United Stock Exchange closed at 44.4675, 44.4625 and 44.4625 respectively, with the total traded volume on the three exchanges at about an average $7.4 billion. (Additional reporting by Neha D'silva; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101021e6ai000v8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
