\par\par \b \uc2 SNAPSHOT-Indian policy highlights on Friday, Oct 15\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 06:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Oct 15 (Reuters) - Following are statements from Indian policymakers as well as the latest news and scheduled events.\par \par \uc2 * Denotes new entry.\par \par \uc2 * India must manage capital inflows so that it can fund its current account deficit while at the same time not harming exports, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor said late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that we have capital inflows that at some point are substantially larger than our current account deficit means there is a pressure on the rupee to appreciate," \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said at a Bloomberg-UTV event.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister said the government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if exorbitant interest rates offered by microfinance institutions were not lowered, the Business Standard reported on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The cost of intermediation should be reduced," the report quoted Pranab Mukherjee as saying.\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS:\par \par \uc2 * India has attracted a record $22.5 billion in inflows into equities this year, putting upward pressure on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of September, the rupee <INR=IN> has appreciated 6.7 percent, reaching a 25-month high.\par \par \uc2 India's current account deficit <INCURA=ECI> widened sharply to $13.7 billion in the April-June quarter from $4.5 billion year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on Thursday in reportedly its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. [ID:nSGE69D0EX]\par \par \uc2 * Microfinance institutions (MFIs) extend small loans to some of India's poorest people who are unable to obtain banking credit, but reportedly charge interest rates of up to 28 percent.\par \par \uc2 Muhammad Yunus, the Nobel Prize-winning pioneer of microfinance, has warned that profit-making MFIs are no different from loan-sharking moneylenders.\par \par \uc2 In August, Indian lender \uc2 SKS Microfinance\uc2  raised about $358 million in a heavily-oversubscribed IPO, signalling strong investor appetite for the sector. [ID:nSGE67209X]\par \par \uc2 With a potential base of 120 million unbanked homes, India's likely microfinance credit demand of about $270 billion is the highest in the world.\par \par \uc2 SCHEDULED EVENTS THIS WEEK:\par \par \uc2 FRIDAY, Oct. 15\par \par \uc2 ------------------\par \par \uc2 Data: WPI Inflation at 12 p.m. (0630 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Data: \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at 5 p.m. (1130 GMT) (Compiled by Henry Foy in NEW DELHI; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-POLICY/SNAPSHOT|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101015e6af00089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
