\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-RBI FOCUS-IPO flows may force cbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 04:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats story issued late on Wednesday)\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2  * \uc2 Coal \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $3.5 bln IPO to trigger more inflows\par \par \uc2  * RBI typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to manage volatility\par \par \uc2  * Cbank not seen favouring capital controls\par \par \uc2  By Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Tony Munroe\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Oct 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets but may be forced to in coming weeks as foreign investors pour in billions of dollars to buy shares in the country's largest ever IPO.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investment in Indian stocks stands at a record $21.8 billion and more than a third of that flowed in since the start of September, pushing the rupee to a two-year high last week.\par \par \uc2 Coal India\uc2 's $3.5 billion share sale next week could prove the tipping point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if, as expected, it generates heavy demand, although \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  sources downplayed any intention to manage inflows and ease pressure on the rupee.\par \par \uc2  "We are not traders. We don't buy dollars and sell dollars alternately. The volatility will be temporary and exporters and importers will take care of the levels," said an official, who is directly involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't entirely dismiss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  though. Officials said the RBI, as always, stands ready to manage any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and Governor Duvvuri Subbarao indicated in Washington over the weekend that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if inflows are "lumpy and volatile".\par \par \uc2  That's exactly what India may get from the \uc2 Coal India\uc2  IPO, which is expected to be popular given the company's dominant market position and because a lower-then-expected price band for the share offer could result in heavy oversubscription.\par \par \uc2  "As of now, we don't intend to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as this is just a temporary issue of flows coming in and going out," the RBI official said, declining to be identified.\par \par \uc2  "The governor's statement was a weapon to calm down markets and ensure there is no panic. It doesn't necessarily mean we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by us is a big thing," the source said.\par \par \uc2  <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Coal India\uc2 's IPO                            [ID:nSGE69C09B]\par \par \uc2  Breakingviews column on IPO flows           [ID:nLDE69B0V2]\par \par \uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2  Half the \uc2 Coal India\uc2  shares will be sold to institutions, with the majority of such demand expected to come from overseas.\par \par \uc2  Under new rules introduced this year, institutional investors must prefund in full the IPO shares they want to buy. Previously, they had to provide 10 percent up front.\par \par \uc2  If the institutional part of the IPO is five times subscribed and foreign funds account for 70 percent of such demand, it would draw more than $6 billion in additional funds into India -- or the equivalent of more than a quarter of the record overseas funds that have already invested in stocks this year.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Coal India\uc2  offer will open to institutions from Oct 18-20 and shares will be allocated within 12 working days of the closing. Refunds of unallocated funds are expected to head back out of India, while IPO proceeds will go into government coffers.\par \par \uc2  "Given we will likely see lumpy U.S. dollar inflows first, followed by a part of that going back, we should have RBI watching the market very carefully. Will not be surprised if RBI does come in to smooth the flows out," said Ananth Narayan G, head of fixed income, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commodities-South Asia at Standard Chartered.\par \par \uc2  YIELD QUEST\par \par \uc2  Sluggish economies and ultra-low interest rates in developed countries have sent a flood of return-hungry funds to emerging markets, putting upward pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prompting many central banks to step in to brake the appreciation.\par \par \uc2  Brazil's \uc2 Petrobras\uc2    last month raised $70 billion in the world's largest share sale, adding to inflows already chasing double-digit interest rates and pushing the real <BRL=> to two year peaks.\par \par \uc2  Last week, Brazil doubled a tax on foreign investment in bonds to 4 percent, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stepping up buying of dollars.\par \par \uc2  Subbarao indicated in Washington, where he attended a meeting of the International Monetary Fund, that he did not support capital controls.\par \par \uc2  "Capital controls can be gamed or circumvented. Also stop-go policies send wrong signals to potential investors," he said.\par \par \uc2  In 2009, the RBI sold a net $5.8 billion to prevent the rupee from falling below a record low of 52.2, but traders believe it has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2  "There are costs associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because we will have to also sterilise the money," the RBI source said.\par \par \uc2  The rupee is up 5.3 percent since September. Last year, record inflows of $17.5 billion pushed it up by 4.7 percent.\par \par \uc2  More state share sales will further test India's tolerance for inflows. \uc2 Power Grid Corp\uc2   and \uc2 Hindustan Copper\uc2   aim to raise a combined $2.8 billion by year-end.\par \par \uc2  On the face of it, India would welcome inflows -- if they are stable. The April-June current account showed a record deficit and on the capital account, foreign direct investment is down this year.\par \par \uc2  "Our absorptive capacity for inflows has risen as our current account deficit is growing," a second \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, who declined to be identified, told Reuters.  (Editing by Neil Fullick)    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENTRALBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT)|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101014e6ae0003u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
