\par\par \b \uc2 SNAPSHOT-Indian policy highlights on Monday, Oct 11\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2010\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Oct 11 (Reuters) - Following are statements from Indian policymakers as well as the latest news and scheduled events.\par \par \uc2 * Denotes new entry.\par \par \uc2 * India has delayed the release of its September headline inflation data <INWPI=ECI> by a day to Friday, a trade and industry ministry spokesman said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 India is unlikely to deregulate diesel prices while inflation is high, television channel CNBC TV-18 reported on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think it will be very wise or prudent thing to do (to deregulate diesel prices) at a time when inflation is running so high," India's Finance Secretary Ashok Chawla told CNBC TV-18.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed to maintain stability, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said during a panel discussion at the International Monetary Fund in Washington on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 "If the inflows are lumpy and volatile or if they disrupt the macroeconomic situation, we will do so," \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS:\par \par \uc2 * The WPI data release would be delayed by a day as government offices in the capital city would be shut for the Oct. 14 closing ceremony of the 12-day Commonwealth Games, the spokesman told Reuters on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The data is usually released on the 14th day of each month or the next working day, if it falls on a weekend or a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 In June, India allowed oil firms to set petrol prices and raised prices of diesel, kerosene and cooking gas. It also decided to free up diesel prices without specifying any time frame for its implementation. [ID:nSGE65O0AS]\par \par \uc2 India's headline inflation stood at 8.5 percent in August, above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone of 5-6 percent and compared with the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's end-March 2011 projection of 6 percent, when the current financial year ends.\par \par \uc2 Foreign institutional investors have pumped a record $21.3 billion into Indian equities so far this year, helping push the rupee <INR=IN> to a 25-month high last week.\par \par \uc2 The RBI, which typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to soften sharp moves in the partially convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the recent rally. [ID:nSGE69902W]\par \par \uc2 Last week, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said there was currently no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign portfolio inflows.\par \par \uc2 SCHEDULED EVENTS THIS WEEK:\par \par \uc2 TUESDAY, Oct. 12\par \par \uc2 -------------------\par \par \uc2 Data: Industrial output at 11 a.m. (0530 GMT)\par \par \uc2 FRIDAY, Oct. 15\par \par \uc2 ------------------\par \par \uc2 Data: WPI Inflation at 12 p.m. (0630 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Data: \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at 5 p.m. (1130 GMT) (Compiled by Henry Foy in NEW DELHI; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-POLICY/SNAPSHOT (UPDATE)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101011e6ab0006z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
