\par\par \b \uc2 AT A GLANCE: Officials Warn  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Fight Can Undermine Global Economy\b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 20:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 THE NEWS: A number of high-ranking officials spoke out Thursday on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  battles that have spurred tensions around the globe, with International Monetary Fund Managing Director Dominique Strauss-Kahn warning that such conflict can undermine the world economy.\par \par \uc2 A day after U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner essentially accused China of sparking a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war, Strauss-Kahn said the IMF needs to launch a "systemic stability initiative" to build international consensus on global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Also Thursday, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels should reflect economic fundamentals, while World Bank head Robert Zoellick said multilateral bodies have a role to play in resolving \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions but that, ultimately, countries must tackle the issue by rebalancing their economies.\par \par \uc2 COUNTRIES ON \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 : China is committed to moving toward a flexible exchange rate regime, but the pace \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform has to be gradual, a People's Bank of China official said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may move to cap gains in the rupee if it rises to 43-42 against the U.S. dollar, though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely at current levels, a senior finance ministry official said after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 25-month high against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique de Campos Meirelles said that a combination of U.S. policies, European economics and China's fixed exchange rate has led to major distortions in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 THE MARKETS: The U.S. dollar recovered from a broad slump against most of its rivals as investors pared bets on riskier assets ahead of Friday's reading on the U.S. employment situation.\par \par \uc2 Thursday afternoon, the euro was at $1.3877 from $1.3929 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as $1.4030. The dollar was at Y82.43 from Y82.96, after falling as low as Y82.11, while the euro was at Y114.40 from Y115.55. The U.K. pound was at $1.5872 from $1.5885. The dollar was at CHF0.9690 from CHF0.9618.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index was at 77.587 from 77.435, rebounding from a dip below 77, its lowest level since January.\par \par \uc2 WHAT THEY'RE SAYING: "Many do consider their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a weapon, and that's certainly not for the good of the global economy," the IMF's Strauss-Kahn said.\par \par \uc2 "The current policies of the developed countries is leading to very significant capital flows into some of the emerging countries. This is putting upward pressure on exchange rates," said South African Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan, who heads the Group of 24 emerging and developing countries.\par \par \uc2 "More than ever, I think that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals," the ECB's Trichet said. "Excess volatility ... [has] adverse implications for economic and financial stability."\par \par \uc2 Dow Jones's coverage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation includes:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G-24 Calls For Global Coordination On Macroeconomic Policies \par Strauss-Kahn: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Contrary To Global Rebalancing Efforts \par World Bank Zoellick: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tensions Can Lead To Trouble If Not Managed \par Trichet: "Occasion" For \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Talks In Washington \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Dollar Recovers From Slump; US Payroll Data Eyed \par Brazil \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Eyes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Market Distortions \par Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Buys Dollars In Auction At BRL1.6782 \par PBOC Deputy Governor: Committed To Flexible Exchange Rate Regime \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Official: RBI May \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  If Rupee-Dollar Hits INR43-INR42 \par Turkey \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reserves Up At $77.03 Bln In Week To Oct 1 - IHA \par MARKET TALK: To \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Or Not To \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ? \par Brazil's Real Gains Versus Dollar Despite Government Efforts \par WSJ: China's Yuan Begins Electronic Trading Offshore \par MARKETWATCH VIEW: It's A Race To The Bottom In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Markets \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 10-07-10 1420ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020101007e6a7000h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
