\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: RBI  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Can't Be Ruled Out -StanChart\b0\par\par\uc2 1,084 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0753 GMT [Dow Jones] While downside risks have increased for USD/INR as it tests key support at 44.15 ahead of $3 billion-$3.5 billion \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . IPO, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support USD can't be ruled out, says Standard Chartered foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Priyanka Chakravarty. "The move in the USD/INR has been rapid and, if it persists, could increase \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concerns regarding volatility and competitiveness (of exports)," Chakravarty says. But in absence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , fate of INR likely to hinge on whether capital inflows for and after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coal India\f28 \uc2 \f2  share sale live up to expectations, as well as whether Fed moves on quantitative easing continue to pressure USD globally. USD/INR at 44.17. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0750 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are bouncing off early lows as equities start to slip. Gilts are also getting support from weak housing data. UK house prices slumped in September by the largest monthly amount since records began in 1983, a survey by Halifax shows. While the BOE is expected to hold its policy rate and its government bond buying program unchanged (announcement at 1100 GMT), minutes due later this month could show a 3-way split in voting. Ahead of the BOE decision, UK industrial production figures are out at 0830 GMT. December gilts are down 0.07 at 124.90 vs 124.71 session low. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0750 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/SEK may rise further Thursday if buying of euros continues on behalf of Renault (RNO.FR) following its sale of a stake in Volvo (VOLV-B.SK) worth about SEK28B says Carl Hammer at SEB. "It seems as though the bulk of the deal has passed through the market but we can't be sure there isn't more to come," says Hammer. EUR/SEK trades at 9.3244. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0748 GMT [Dow Jones] Continued buying of the euro on behalf of Renault (RNO.FR) after its Volvo (VOLV-B.SK) stake sale could drive EUR/SEK higher Thursday, says \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . "\uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  was the sole book runner on the deal and was seen in the market hoovering EUR/SEK," says \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , adding "players will looking for clues that it has finished". EUR/SEK trades at a 1-month high of 9.3337.(charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0739 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY is trading at a fresh 15-year low and bang on the 2-year support line at 82.62 notes \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Karen Jones. She looks for this to hold and provoke a recovery toward the 20-day MA at 84.15 and the 55-day MA at 84.98. Alternatively, a sustained break below 82.62 opens risk toward 80.00. USD/JPY now at 0.8263. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia government bonds mostly tad higher following overnight rally in U.S. Treasurys. Local dealer says volume thin, market players staying on sidelines ahead of reopening of 7-year benchmark MGS, August trade data both due tomorrow. Adds, yields also likely to stay rangebound next week ahead of budget due Friday. Yields for November 2019 MGS down 1 bp at 3.64%, September 2017 MGS flat at 3.56%, August 2015 MGS down 2 bps at 3.24%. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT [Dow Jones] French August foreign trade figures point to robust economic activity in August and to very dynamic 3Q trade, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  senior economist Dominique Barbet. 3Q exports and imports would both gain 7.5% on the quarter if export and import levels remain unchanged in September, which is a conservative hypothesis, says Barbet. (william.horobin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0736 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD stays in tight range, amid absence of leads with China markets closed a week for National Day holiday, only resuming activity tomorrow, says trader at Singapore bank; tips pair in 7.7540-7.7570 band near-term. "We see sluggish stock moves (HSI down 0.1%), and China markets still closed for today, so there's nothing in particular to draw investors' attention." Pair last at 7.7559, vs 7.7561 in morning, 7.7552 yesterday. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0736 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish zloty is weaker vs the euro, continues its corrective movement from Wednesday. But the zloty's weakness "shouldn't worry, because considering present positive sentiment toward emerging markets' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Poland's strong fundamentals, the zloty shouldn't depreciate too much these days," Raiffeisen says. EUR/PLN trades at 3.9640 from 3.9505 late Wednesday, USD/PLN at 2.8364 from 2.8460. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0736 GMT [Dow Jones] October HSI futures down 0.2% at 22,882, as cash market pulls back (only down 0.1%, after having gained in 20 of previous 24 sessions) to consolidate recent gains. Still, contract trading at premium to cash most of session, now 10-20 points, continuing to flag near-term bullish view. Volume lighter than recent session at 43,224 lots. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0730 GMT [Dow Jones] Stung by a sudden drop in the ruble in recent weeks despite high oil prices, Russia, at least for now, is one of the few countries seeking a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , UralSib Capital says. A stronger ruble trims profits of commodity exporters whose revenues are denominated in dollars, but it can help food retailers, pharmaceutical companies and other parts of the economy that are increasingly importing from Europe and other countries, says UralSib chief strategist Chris Weafer. The ruble has strengthened in recent days amid \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments. It's at 34.88 versus the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket from 34.69 late Wednesday and stronger vs dollar at 29.7001. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0728 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR slips to 25-month low, tracking rally in EUR, but now finding strong support, say traders; pair at 44.20 after slipping to 44.12, vs 44.50 late Wednesday. "The correction is completely in line with the EUR, although the rapid bounce from 44.12 is a bit of a surprise," says trader with private bank. Tips further correction to 43.80 if bounceback not stemming from RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (bijou.george@dowjones.com) [ 10-07-10 0353ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101007e6a70005a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
