\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister: Don't Think RBI Needs To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Now On Rupee Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bijou George  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 13:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now to moderate the rupee's rise, the country's finance minister said Monday, even as huge capital inflows led to a 3.3% rise in the local unit in the September quarter.\par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank is watching it. I do not think just now it (the rupee strengthening) is a cause for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Pranab Mukherjee told local television channel ET Now.\par \par \uc2 "As and when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is called for, Reserve Bank will be doing it."\par \par \uc2 Mukherjee's comments come amid increasing speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may act to slow the rupee's rise even as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  has been adopting a hands-off attitude on the local unit.\par \par \uc2 Lagged RBI data shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for eight months to July 31.\par \par \uc2 This differs from the approaches of other central banks in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Japan, for example, stepped in heavily on Sept. 15 to cut off a yen rally that threatened to hamper the competitiveness of its exports, dumping a massive Y2 trillion in the market.\par \par \uc2 The central banks of Malaysia and Korea have both stepped in intermittently to smoothen the movements of their local units.\par \par \uc2 Traders have been fleeing the greenback, putting in money in riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including that of India, the second-fastest growing major economy in the world.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around INR43-INR44 to a dollar on previous occasions and the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains quite strong if the rupee gains more, said local bond house IDBI Gilts in a note.\par \par \uc2 "As RBI follows the policy of managed float, if the appreciation of INR (rupee) is continued, (an) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by RBI becomes quite likely."\par \par \uc2 Mukherjee also told the news channel that there was no need for the government to consider putting a limit on foreign fund inflows.\par \par \uc2 "There is (a) stable policy regime. We do not change our policy with some sort of knee-jerk reaction," he said.\par \par \uc2 India in fact liberalized its foreign fund rules in September, allowing foreigners to invest more in the country's debt markets.\par \par \uc2 Large capital inflows into the country's stocks have pushed the benchmark 30-share Sensitive Index to a 33-month high. Foreigners pumped in $5.43 billion in September alone.\par \par \uc2 These portfolio flows are crucial to meet the country's gaping current account deficit, but at the same time they could pose a difficulty for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they turn out to be hot money, or short-term flows, chasing returns.\par \par \uc2 But Mukherjee said he doesn't expect any substantial outflows that would create uncertainty as India's economy is growing robustly.\par \par \uc2 He also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't behind the curve in raising interest rates, although he said that persistently high food inflation was a cause of worry.\par \par \uc2 Mukherjee expects food prices to moderate after the festive season and said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must strike a balance between growth and inflation.\par \par \uc2 Food prices in India rose for the fifth-straight week with the food articles index, rising 0.8% to 179.9 in the week ended Sept. 18, latest data showed.\par \par \uc2 Deepak Mohanty, an executive director with the RBI said last week in a speech that food price inflation may acquire a structural character, unless supply-side measures were taken.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already raised the key borrowing rate by 125 basis points, and the key lending rate by 175 basis points so far in 2010 in a bid to anchor inflationary expectations.\par \par \uc2 -By Bijou George, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-22-6145-6111; bijou.george@dowjones.com [ 10-04-10 0725ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020101004e6a400028\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
