 587 bps from 350 bps eight months ago, \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  says; creates negative carry for RBI. Anyway, over long-term, India's widening current account deficit, takes care of this job. Unlike for its peers in the region, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one task off RBI's desk. See: =HEARD ON THE STREET: India Unruffled By The Rupee's Swing (harsh.joshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0448 GMT [Dow Jones]BOJ offers to inject total of Y1.4 trillion into money market at 0400 GMT via both fixed-rate and auction-style \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offers to supply ample amount of funds, with about Y2 trillion fund shortage expected for Friday (Japan markets will be closed Thursday for national holiday), analysts say. BOJ forecast in morning \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account balance to be around Y18.2 trillion. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares shrug off initial fatigue, with interest returning even to blue chips, which have been underperforming lower liners lately. STI +0.6% at 3114.02 midday vs down 0.3% at 3084.89 earlier. Lower liners stronger, with FTSE ST Small Cap Index +1.2%, FTSE ST Mid Cap Index +1.1%. Overall volume robust at 1.98 billion shares worth S$1.39 billion. "Due to the curbs by the government on property investments, money and capital is being diverted to the stock market," says trader; adds, "stay invested. A rising tide will lift all boats." Singapore government last month unveiled third round of housing-market curbs in 12 months in bid to rein in property speculation. Key gainers among blue chips include NOL (N03.SG), +3.5% at S$2.07, \uc2 CapitaLand\uc2  (C31.SG), +2.8% at S$4.09, SGX (S68.SG), +2.4% at S$8.70. Among lower liners, Cosco (F83.SG) +5.2% at S$1.82, Biosensors (B20.SG) +5.2% at S$1.02, CSC (C06.SG) +9.1% at S$0.18. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com) [ 09-