\uc2 's current account balance to be around Y18.2 trillion. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares shrug off initial fatigue, with interest returning even to blue chips, which have been underperforming lower liners lately. STI +0.6% at 3114.02 midday vs down 0.3% at 3084.89 earlier. Lower liners stronger, with FTSE ST Small Cap Index +1.2%, FTSE ST Mid Cap Index +1.1%. Overall volume robust at 1.98 billion shares worth S$1.39 billion. "Due to the curbs by the government on property investments, money and capital is being diverted to the stock market," says trader; adds, "stay invested. A rising tide will lift all boats." Singapore government last month unveiled third round of housing-market curbs in 12 months in bid to rein in property speculation. Key gainers among blue chips include NOL (N03.SG), +3.5% at S$2.07, \uc2 CapitaLand\uc2  (C31.SG), +2.8% at S$4.09, SGX (S68.SG), +2.4% at S$8.70. Among lower liners, Cosco (F83.SG) +5.2% at S$1.82, Biosensors (B20.SG) +5.2% at S$1.02, CSC (C06.SG) +9.1% at S$0.18. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0439 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end +0.1% at 453.9 vs day's high 457.0, on 3Q earnings expectations. But many players still hesitant to enter market, wait to see what new measures to boost cash supply government will introduce; government to hold major meeting to review economic performance for the quarter at end of month. "Everyone has faith that the government will have to introduce stronger measures after it last week raised GDP growth target set for this year to +6.7% vs +6.5%. Also among the possible measures, it is likely to cut interest rates," says analyst. Volume thin at 33.4 million shares valued at VND908 billion exchanging hands. Among most active, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends down 4.8% at VND35,800, Eximbank (EIB.VH) ends flat at VND17,600, \uc2 Quoc Cuong Gia Lai\uc2  (QCG.VH) end +4.7% at VND31,300. Tips more gains tomorrow with key index to move in 455-460 range