\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: No Noticeable ETF Uptick With Gold Spike -Trader\b0\par\par\uc2 1,591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 07:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0503 GMT [Dow Jones] No sign of marked pickup in ETF demand accompanying gold's latest record high, says ETF market-maker with major global bank in Sydney; still, 685 contracts changed hands on Comex's Dec. 2010 contract as metal jumped 0.16% in a minute to $1,292.50/oz record, before sell-off prompted move back below $1,290/oz around 0415 GMT. ETFs increasingly popular channel of commodity exposure for retail investors, hedge funds; lack of activity on that front suggests major producer or dealer responsible for spike rather than hedge fund. (david.fickling@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0500 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold at $1,287.40/oz, up 60 cents and just off all-time intraday high of $1,290.80 hit just after 0400 GMT. Some Comex buying dragging spot higher, says Singapore based trader, who adds early London trade will likely see break of $1,291 and assault on $1,300 psychological target. However says Asian physical market subdued with some sporadic Indian buying but Chinese absent for holiday. "I'm still waiting for a correction," he says. Daily gold chart shows unusually consistent trading pattern since recent trough at $1,158 on July 28, only 12 down days out of 40; biggest one-day decline 0.9% on Sept 9. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0500 GMT [Dow Jones] India overnight call rates higher as liquidity in system still tight, says dealer with state-run bank; interbank call rate on RBI's negotiated dealing system at 6.20% vs 5.90% at Tuesday's close, collateralized borrowing and lending obligation or CBLO at 5.97%, closer to repo rate of 6.00%. "Liquidity continues to remain a constraint and overnight rates will hover at or above the repo rate," says dealer. Tips call rates in 6.00%-6.20% range, CBLO in 5.50%-6.00% in session. Notes, banks likely to borrow INR400 billion at RBI's liquidity auction in day. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0457 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ shares flat at 3230.17, though some heavyweights lower on profit-taking with Fletcher Building (FBU.NZ) down 0.7% at NZ$8.60, Telecom (TEL.NZ) down 1.9% at NZ$2.02, says Hamilton Hindin Greene broker Grant Williamson. Notes Pumpkin Patch (PPL.NZ) flat at NZ$1.95 after reporting in-line FY results. Guinness Peat (GPG.NZ) +1.5% at NZ$0.67 as investors remain upbeat about appointment of 4 new independent directors. But overall, "it's a relatively quiet day. There is not a lot of turnover, just a little bit of profit-taking and no clear direction." Says investors will remain focused on offshore markets for cues. While tough to predict how markets may go later in global trading day; "you would have to say the trend is certainly positive at the moment." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0456 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR extends fall to fresh 13-year low of 3.0910 vs 3.1000 late Tuesday; two dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted buying dollars at 3.0910. "Bank Negara is buying in small doses to smoothen the flow...volume is a bit thinner today compared with yesterday," says one dealer. Tips immediate support at 3.0900; then 3.0750 (October 17, 1997 low) in medium term. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0455 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei 225 December futures flat at 9530 amid relatively low participation levels as China markets are closed, Japan markets close tomorrow for holiday; while USD/JPY hovering below 85, investors stay alert that government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (again). "Investors are worried about the possibi