\par\par \b \uc2 Indian shares hit fresh 32-mth high on foreign fund inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 788 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 07:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * BSE Sensex up 0.8 pct; Reliance, IT stocks help rally\par \par \uc2 * Foreign fund inflows at $14.3 bln so far this year\par \par \uc2 * Financials mixed ahead of cbank policy review on Thursday (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Bharghavi Nagaraju\par \par \uc2 BANGALORE, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Indian shares reset 32-month highs for the fourth straight session on Wednesday driven by continued robust foreign fund inflows and a catch-up rally in index-heavyweight \uc2 Reliance Industries Ltd\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 India's top software services exporters, which derive more than half their revenue from the United States, joined the party as promising U.S. retail sales data boosted optimism over recovery in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The market took in its stride India's widening trade gap, which stood at a 23-month high in August, and a higher deficit outlook for the financial year ending March 2011. But, the trade secretary said the bulging deficit was not yet a problem and could be financed. [ID:nSGE68E0AH].\par \par \uc2 The 30-share BSE index <.BSESN> ended up 0.8 percent at 19,502.11 points, with 17 of its components advancing. It hit a high of 19,554.50 points, its highest since January 2008.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign institutional investor money is what is driving the market as of now and will continue to drive as long as there is no major upheaval in the international markets," said Ambareesh Baliga, vice president at \uc2 Karvy Stock Broking\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "When money is chasing growth, it is difficult for us to fix a valuation for the market. It is the money that decides the valuation."\par \par \uc2 India, Asia's third-largest economy, is expected to surpass government estimates for an 8.5 percent growth in 2010/11 boosted by a surprise 13.8 percent jump in factory output in July.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have poured in $14.3 billion into Indian stocks so far this year helping the benchmark index rise 11.7 percent. In 2009, a record foreign fund inflow of $17.6 billion led to an 81-percent surge in the index.\par \par \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2 , which was down 9.3 percent this year until Tuesday on concerns over diversification into non-core businesses and delay in ramp-up of gas production, surged up 2.3 percent to close at 1,010.45 rupees.\par \par \uc2 Tata Consultancy Services\uc2  and \uc2 Infosys Technologies\uc2  , India's top two technology firms, scaled new highs earlier in the day. TCS closed up 2.2 percent, while \uc2 Infosys\uc2  and No. 3 ranked Wipro rose 2.5 percent and 2.3 percent respectively.\par \par \uc2 Financials closed mixed ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-quarter policy review on Thursday, when the bank is widely expected to raise key interest rates by 25 basis points. [nSGE68E09E].\par \par \uc2 Top lenders \uc2 State Bank of India\uc2  and ICICI Bank closed down 1.7 percent and 0.1 percent respectively. \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  and mortgage lender \uc2 Housing Development Finance Corp\uc2  bucked the trend notching up 1.8 percent and 1.3 precent gains respectively.\par \par \uc2 Vehicles maker \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  hit a new high in at least 20 years for the second straight session before a lower-than-expected 29-percent rise in August global vehicle sales pushed the shares down 2.9 percent at close.\par \par \uc2 Top utility vehicle \uc2 Mahindra & Mahindra\uc2  also scaled a record high and ended up 0.95 percent. Leading car maker Maruti Suzuki gained 1.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 In the broader market, losers led gainers in a ratio of 1.4:1 on volume of 558.2 million shares.\par \par \uc2 The 50-share NSE index <.NSEI> was up 1.1 percent at 5,860.95 points.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the MSCI's measure of Asian markets other than Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> was up 0.4 percent, while Japan's Nikkei <.N225> rose 2.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 STOCK ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Pioneer Distilleries\uc2  hit the 5-percent upper limit for the second session at 76.10 rupees, after United Spirits said on Tuesday it had agreed to buy a 54.7-percent stake in the company at 101 rupees a share. [ID:nBMA008439]\par \par \uc2 MAIN TOP 3 BY VOLUME\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Karuturi Global\uc2  on 25.3 million shares\par \par \uc2 * NHPC on 6.7 million shares\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Ispat Industries\uc2  on 6.1 million shares\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH * For technical analysis double click on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.reutersindia.net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.reutersindia.net}}}\uc2  * India rupee report [INR/] * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond report [IN/] * Dollar soars, yen falls as Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  [FRX/] * U.S. crude futures fall $1 to $75.80/bbl [O/R] * Yen drops, Nikkei up on Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  [MKTS/GLOB] * Wall Street futures signal mixed open; data eyed [.N] * For closing rates of Indian ADRs <INADR>\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-STOCKS/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|E|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000ak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
