\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Gains As China's Yuan Move Fuels Risk Appetite; Bonds Down\b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2010\par 16:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                      As Of 1200 GMT \par                      Latest      Change \par    USD/INR           45.76        -0.41 \par    7.80% 2020 Bond   7.57%        +1 BP \par    8.20% 2022 Bond   7.93%        -3 BPs \par    Call Rate         5.40%        +20 BPs \par    Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    May               1.24         -0.0525 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee Monday rose to its highest level against the U.S. dollar in a month, in line with other Asian peers as China's decision to ease the yuan's peg to the greenback boosted local stocks and encouraged investors to buy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  perceived riskier.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at INR45.76 in late trade, down from INR46.17 in late Friday trade. This was the dollar's lowest level since May 18, when it touched INR45.51.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Thailand, Indonesia and South Korea gained after the People's Bank of China said Saturday it would allow the yuan to gradually rise against the dollar. Beijing had pegged the yuan at CNY6.83 to a dollar since July 2008 to protect its export sector amid the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 China's decision buoyed stock markets across Asia, with the \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's Sensitive Index rising 1.7% to close at 17,876.55.\par \par \uc2 While the central banks in South Korea and Thailand are suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away from the market.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI's absence from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may also make the rupee particularly well placed to gain from the yuan de-pegging," Standard Chartered Bank said in a report.\par \par \uc2 "Given that the USD/INR (pair) is likely to convincingly breach INR46.00, the market will now focus on the 100-day moving average, which is at 45.70," it added.\par \par \uc2 Top Indian policy makers said it is too early to judge the impact of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move on the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "What happens to the exchange rate, we are evaluating the impact and that in turn will have an impact on trade and capital flows. So I think we have got to wait for some time and see how this plays out," RBI Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 Finance Secretary Ashok Chawla said the government will "wait and watch" the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move on the economy. China is one of India's largest trading partners, enjoying a $15.2 billion trade surplus during April-December 2009, according to latest data.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, government bonds ended mixed as strong demand for funds to pay for Internet bandwidth licenses strained liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.80% 2020 bond closed at INR101.58, down from INR101.64 at Friday's close. However, the second-most traded 8.20% 2022 bond finished higher at INR102.00 from INR101.81 at last close.\par \par \uc2 The market didn't draw any comfort from Gokarn's comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could consider additional measures to ease liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "What I want to emphasise is that this (tight liquidity) is temporary. This is money that is accruing in government accounts, which will be spent, which will find its way back into the system. (It is) not a permanent structural change in the system," he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Nupur Acharya, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-22-61456117; nupur.acharya@dowjones.com [ 21-06-10 1430GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100621e66l00136\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
