\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-SCENARIOS-India rupee may rise despite interim hurdles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Swati Bhat   \par \uc2 905 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2010\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story issued late on Tuesday)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 1 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee is getting battered alongside regional peers and is likely to remain volatile until the euro zone uncertainty draws to a close but it is still expected to gain over fiscal year 2010/11.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee is among Asia's five worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2010 having shed 6.3 percent from the year's high of 44.18, after out-performing rivals last year.\par \par \uc2 The unit shed 4.3 percent in May largely weighed by foreign funds withdrawing around $2 billion from the local stock market, in their biggest single-month pullout since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 India is far less dependant on exports than some of its Asian peers, which insulates it somewhat from external shocks.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and traders believe the rupee will continue to remain volatile and there is a possibility that it may even revisit record low levels of 52.2 per dollar touched in early March 2009 on the back of a sustained risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Here are some scenarios on the rupee's outlook:\par \par \uc2 RUPEE WEAKENS FURTHER IN THE NEAR-TERM\par \par \uc2 The most likely scenario. Almost all emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are under pressure amid the global flight to safety and the rupee is unlikely to be an exception.\par \par \uc2 It is seen closely tracking moves in domestic equities and the euro in the near-term with the bias clearly towards further weakness. A widening current-account deficit adds to downside risk.\par \par \uc2 "There is no strong momentum for sustainability of near term gains in EUR/USD and in domestic bourses into the short/medium term," said J.Moses Harding, head of global markets at \uc2 IndusInd Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said importers should stay hedged on possible near term rupee gains towards 46.00-46.10 and 45.75-45.85, while exporters should sell at 46.55-46.65 and then at 46.75-46.85.\par \par \uc2 If the current bout of global risk aversion persists, the rupee may drop towards record lows before heading back to a path of longer-term appreciation based on capital inflows and the economy's growth prospects, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO PREVENT SHARP SWINGS IN RUPEE\par \par \uc2 Only if the rupee is an outlier. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the unit falls or rises sharply on any single-day as long as it moves in line with fundamentals, but it will step in to curb speculative flows from fueling volatility.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's official view is that it is agnostic on the value of the rupee.\par \par \uc2 A weak rupee would help exporters and as long as the unit moves on fundamental factors and not hot money flows, the RBI is unlikely to step in.\par \par \uc2 Hence the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smoothen flows but will not be influencing the rupee's moves in any way.\par \par \uc2 RUPEE GAINS TOWARDS 43.50-44.00 BY END OF FY11\par \par \uc2 A likely scenario, assuming a normal summer monsoon helps growth and attracts foreign capital, boosting the rupee.\par \par \uc2 Europe is the wild card. If the situation there settles down, risk-appetite may return with India attracting foreign investment thanks to robust economic growth, which is forecast this year to reach 8.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners, despite the large sales of Indian stocks in May, are still net buyers of $4.6 billion worth of shares in 2010, adding to last year's record inflows of $17.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 India's economy grew at its fastest in six months in the quarter through March thanks to government and consumer spending, which was roughly in line with expectations and likely to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its path of gradual monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 Policy tightening would in turn support the rupee as rate differentials between India and developed economies could rise and attract more foreign funds, with most economists expecting the rupee to end the fiscal year 2010/11 at around 43.5 to 44 levels against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally nothing has changed for India. So when the dust settles and investors re-focus on local fundamentals, we are likely to witness a clearer acceleration in INR gains," said Priyanka Chakravarty, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered.\par \par \uc2 RUPEE DEPRECIATES ON BROAD DOLLAR RALLY\par \par \uc2 A possibility given safe-haven buying of dollar assets amid Europe's woes and a recovering U.S. economy. If U.S. recovery gains momentum, the dollar may see a broad rally versus majors and emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A sustained crisis in the eurozone would also boost the dollar's appreciation prospects.\par \par \uc2 This could weigh on the rupee, pushing it towards 48-49 per dollar levels by end-March 2011.\par \par \uc2 One could look to trade this view by buying dollar on dips to 45.90, and adding on a move towards 45.45, with stop-loss below 44.75, looking for a move to 48.09 and possibly 49.05.\par \par \uc2 One-year onshore forward rates <INR1Y=> suggest a 2.3 percent depreciation in the rupee from current levels, but those expectations were much higher at 2.9 percent at the end of March, suggesting the market is becoming less bearish about the rupee. (Additional reporting by Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Krishna Kumar in Sydney; Editing by Jason Webb, Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (SCENARIOS, REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100602e6620003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
