\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India FX intervention \highlight\uc2  may be called for-adviser\b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2010\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to recast lede, adds details, quote, background)\par \par \uc2 KOLKATA, May 14 (Reuters) - India's chief economic adviser to the finance ministry on Friday called for some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the rupee's appreciation against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I am not in favour of increasing capital controls. May be this is the kind of situation where some open market action to counter the exchange rate appreciation is called for. But this is something we have to think about," Kaushik Basu said in the eastern Indian city of Kolkata.\par \par \uc2 Basu said the rupee's sharp rise against the U.S. dollar is putting huge pressure on exporters, adding that in the 2009/10 financial year ended March 31, the rupee has strengthened 12.6 percent against the dollar and 8.3 percent against the euro year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 has not interevened in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from December to March, the longest hiatus since mid-2006, triggering views of greater tolerance level for larger gyrations of the Indian unit by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSGE64D01P]\par \par \uc2 So far in 2010, the rupee has risen by 3.1 percent against the dollar on the back of nearly $6 billion net capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "RBI's policy is (the) right kind of policy, it is not to try to buck the trend if it is a permanent change taking place," Basu said.\par \par \uc2 "But here, there is a change which seems like fluctuation there is a reason to believe right now what is happening is a bit of fluctuation. So some attempt that market place action to correct this is indeed called for."\par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> touched a record low of 52.2 per dollar in early March 2009, and since then has gained 15.6 percent. It currently trades at 45.15 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Basu also said he expects India's headline inflation to ease in coming months and food inflation to ease gradually.\par \par \uc2 "It is very very unlikely that inflation will go back to double digits. In June, it might increase slightly due to base effect," he said.\par \par \uc2 India's wholesale price index <INWPI=ECI> rose an annual 9.59 percent in April, driven by high food and fuel prices, government data showed on Friday, lower than March's annual rise of 9.90 percent. [ID:nSGE64D08O] (Reporting by Niladri Bhattacharya, writing by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/ADVISER (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100514e65e002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
