\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank says did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in Feb\b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2010\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story released late Tuesday)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, April 13 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not buy or sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the third straight month in February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had been fairly volatile in February, moving both ways, and traded in a range of 46.865-45.94 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 In 2009, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $5.8 billion to prevent the rupee from depreciating sharply.\par \par \uc2 Though the rupee had dropped to a record low of 52.2 per dollar in early March 2009, yet it ended the fiscal year 2009/10 up 4.7 percent helped by large foreign fund inflows along with periodic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From April to February, the first 11 months of the 2009/10 fiscal year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a net seller of $2.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the partially convertible rupee <INR=D2> closed at 44.48/49 per dollar, off the day's low of 44.68, but still a tad lower than its 44.47/48 close on Monday. It had touched a high of 44.18 on Monday, its strongest since Sept. 8, 2008. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT)|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100414e64e00058\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\sh