\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee firm but off fresh 19-mth high\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2010\par 05:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Profit-booking expected; rupee seen easing to 44.80\par \par \uc2  * No \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently: traders  (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, April 7 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was trading firm on Wednesday but off a 19-month-high as mild profit-booking offset a rise in local shares, and traders said state-run banks were not actively buying the dollar.\par \par \uc2  At 10:25 a.m. (0455 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.37/38 per dollar after hitting 44.31, its strongest since Sept. 8, 2008. It had ended at 44.45/46 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  "The rupee movement seems flow specific ... the market seems oversold to me and over the next two days you should see a pullback to 44.80," said a trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2  Dealers said state-run banks were not actively buying the dollar, implying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not currently looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further appreciation despite the rupee's recent rally.\par \par \uc2  The rupee climbed 2.7 percent in March, its biggest monthly gain since May 2009, on the back of foreign portfolio inflows of about $4.4 billion, and has strengthened a further 1.3 percent since then.\par \par \uc2  Latest data from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in December and January.\par \par \uc2  Stronger Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also supported the rupee. For a snapshot on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , see [EMRG/FRX].\par \par \uc2  India's main stock index <.BSESN> climbed above 18,000 points for the first time since February 2008 and rupee traders said they were positive on stocks in the near term, indicating they expected foreign portfolio inflows to remain robust.\par \par \uc2  One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts <PNDF> were at 44.37/47, near the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market <INRFUTURES>, the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange and MCX-SX were both quoting at 44.4675.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the index of the dollar <.DXY> against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2  The euro struggled, plagued by fresh worries about debt-laden Greece, while commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Australian and Canadian dollars held gains on the back of expectations of higher interest rates. [USD/]  (Reporting by Jeanette Rodrigues; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100410e6470001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
