\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/ \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Real Time: The Meaning of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2010\par 10:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's India Real Time Report blog at blogs.wsj.com/indiarealtime.)\par \par \uc2 Posted by Abhrajit Gangopadhyay\par \par \uc2 It must be some law of finance akin to Murphy's Law that says whenever officials aren't predicted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, they do.\par \par \uc2 Sure enough, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  was reported by Dow Jones Newswires to be suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tuesday morning, buying dollars at 44.35 rupees.\par \par \uc2 But that's not to say the broader point has changed. Traders and analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been caused either by a desire to slow (but not reverse) the rupee's rise, or as a warning to those who might be tempted to think that the rupee's movements will only be one way - and plan their trading strategies accordingly - that the RBI retains the power to surprise.\par \par \uc2 "The RBI was probably a bit uncomfortable with the speed of the rally, so it probably moved in to smooth things out a bit," one trader with a foreign bank told Dow Jones.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the RBI's actions are mostly aimed at smoothing the rupee-dollar volatility and not pegging the rupee to any specific level. Only if the dollar weakens towards 43 rupees is the bank expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The RBI neither confirms nor denies \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but its actions are reflected in data that come out with a month's lag.\par \par \uc2 Pure coincidence, we're sure, that the bank's efforts to buy dollars came just as U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner touched down in Delhi for an official visit to India.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 . [ 06-04-10 0828GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100406e646000ll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
