\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA NEWS HIGHLIGHTS:Top Economic/Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2010\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: COAL INDIA EXPECTS TO LAUNCH IPO IN JULY - CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coal India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest coal producer by output, expects to launch its initial public offer in July and list its shares in August, the state-run company's chairman said. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDIA CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIKELY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - DEALERS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by buying dollars to halt the rupee's gains, three dealers said Tuesday. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA JANUARY-MARCH PRIVATE EQUITY INVESTMENTS RISE TO $2 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Private equity firms' investments in India rose at its fastest pace in 18 months in the January-March period to $2 billion, Venture Intelligence said Tuesday. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TEMASEK STILL IN TALKS WITH INDIA GMR TO BUY ENERGY SHARES -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Singapore state investment firm, is still in "advanced discussions" with India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 GMR Infrastructure Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to buy a stake in its energy unit, said Wong Kim Yin, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Temasek\f28 \uc2 \f2 's managing director for investment. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WELSPUN GUJARAT IN TALKS TO PICK UP STAKE IN SAUDI COMPANY - EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Welspun Gujarat Stahl Rohren Ltd. --a mid-sized steel pipe maker--is in talks to pick up equity in Saudi Arabia-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aziz Pipes Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a Welspun executive said Tuesday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HINDUSTAN PETROLEUM AIMS TO RAISE AT LEAST INR5 BLN VIA BONDS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Petroleum Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . aims to raise at least INR5 billion through bonds, two people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UNITED PHOSPHORUS AIMS TO RAISE INR3 BLN VIA BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Phosphorus Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . aims to raise INR3 billion by selling bonds, a person familiar with the development said Tuesday. (published 0547 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DRUVA SOFTWARE GETS $5 MLN FUNDING FROM SEQUOIA, INDIAN ANGEL NETWORK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Druva Software has received $5 million in funding from Sequoia Capital and Indian Angel Network to finance its expansion in global markets, the company said Tuesday. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par       ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =CHARTING INDIA: DECCAN CHRONICLE MAY RALLY TO INR180.05 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deccan Chronicle Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . appears to have resumed its short-term uptrend, and charts suggest that the stock could rally to the March 22 swing high of INR180.05. (published 0316 GMT) [ 04-06-10 0300ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62501   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100406e6460004f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
