\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank says did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mkt in Jan\b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, March 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not buy or sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin showed.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI)\uc2 , also did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in December. The RBI data was released late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had been volatile in January moving both ways, and traded in a wide range of 46.62 to 45.285, which was its strongest level since September 2008.\par \par \uc2 In 2009 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $5.8 billion to prevent the rupee from depreciating sharply.\par \par \uc2 In early March 2009, the rupee had dropped to a record low of 52.2 per dollar but ended the year up 4.7 percent helped by large foreign fund inflows.\par \par \uc2 From April to January, the first 10 months of the 2009/10 fiscal year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a net seller of $2.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday at 0500 GMT, the partially convertible rupee <INR=D2> was trading at 45.46/47 per dollar, weaker than its previous close of 45.375/385. (Reporting by Swati Bhat ; Editing by Surojit Gupta)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 D