\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Large inflows may help rupee rise -  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  adviser\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2010\par 14:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  mkt must be an exception, not rule\par \par \uc2 * Fiscal consolidation easier in period of price stability (Updates with quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2 By Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Neha D'silva\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Despite a significant current account shortfall the Indian rupee may rise on the back of large capital inflows, the prime minister's economic advisory panel chairman said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Capital inflows have come to dominate the balance of payments and exchange rate may begin to appreciate, even if there is a significant current account deficit because of capital flows," C. Rangarajan said in a prepared speech that was circulated ahead of an event.\par \par \uc2 So far in 2010 foreigners have been net sellers of about $500 million of equities, after they moved in $17.5 billion in 2009 and analysts expect India to attract inflows going ahead.\par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> is up 0.7 percent so far this year, after having risen 4.7 percent in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Rangarajan said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market must be an exception and not a rule.\par \par \uc2 "No \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  can afford to ignore prolonged volatility or mis-alignment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Rangarajan, who once headed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 has said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent excessive volatility but does not target any specific level on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The extent of accumulation of reserves and degree of sterilisation influences the growth of money supply and the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to take a view on the permissible expansion of money supply in the context of large capital inflows," Rangarajan said.\par \par \uc2 India is set to unveil the national budget on Feb. 26 and economists are expecting the government will start its move towards fiscal consolidation by withdrawing some of its stimulus measures introduced to help the economy during the global crisis.\par \par \uc2 Rangarajan said fiscal consolidation becomes easier in an environment of reasonable price stability.\par \par \uc2 Headline inflation in January accelerated to its fastest pace in more than a year, vaulting above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's end-March forecast and putting more pressure on the RBI to raise borrowing rates. [ID:nnSGE61E06Z]\par \par \uc2 "Tying central banks to a specific target of inflation may be too restrictive and may even be counter-productive," he said.\par \par \uc2 RBI Governor Duvvuri Subbarao had said last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot just focus on inflation while formulating the monetary policy as growth was also a concern for a developing country like India. [ID:nBMA006986]\par \par \uc2 Rangarajan said asset prices should also be a key input while framing the monetary policy. (Writing by Swati Bhat; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-ADVISER/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100216e62g000sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100