\par\par \b \uc2 INDIA NEWS HIGHLIGHTS:Top Economic/Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 10:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBI SUBBARAO: TO MEASURE EXTENT OF DUBAI CRISIS, IMPACT ON INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will measure the extent of the Dubai crisis and its impact on India. (published 0732 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NO MATERIAL IMPACT ON INDIA BANK SECTOR FROM DUBAI DEBT CRISIS - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dubai World's debt problems won't have any material impact on India's banking sector, a senior Indian government official said Friday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBI GOPINATH: WILL ASK BANKS TO REPORT EXPOSURE TO DUBAI WORLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will ask banks to report their exposure to Dubai World, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deputy Governor Shyamala Gopinath\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0740 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STATE BANK OF INDIA EXECUTIVE: NO EXPOSURE IN DUBAI WORLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no exposure in Dubai World, Dubai's largest corporate entity, a senior executive at India's largest bank by assets said Friday. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ICICI BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2 : NO MATERIAL EXPOSURE TO NON-INDIAN COMPANIES IN DUBAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ICICI Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has no material exposure to non-Indian companies in Dubai, a spokesman said Friday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: OMAXE LIKELY TO EXIT 2 REALTY PROJECTS IN DUBAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Omaxe Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will likely exit two residential projects in Dubai because it is yet to get possession of land from Dubai's real-estate company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nakheel PJSC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0825 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DLF EXECUTIVE: HAVEN'T MADE ANY INVESTMENT IN DUBAI UNTIL NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DLF Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., India's biggest property developer by sales, said Friday it hasn't made any investment in Dubai's realty market. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA OCTOBER EXPORTS SLUMP SLOWS, GROWTH LIKELY BY MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's merchandise exports shrank in October--the thirteenth consecutive month of decline--but a slowing pace of fall raises hope of exports trending up by March, the federal commerce and industry minister said Friday. (published 0826 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA RBI: CAPITAL INFLOWS SHOULD BE EQUAL TO CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India Governor Duvvuri Subbarao said Friday that capital inflows into the country should be equivalent or slightly in excess to the country's current account deficit. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RBI LIKELY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - DEALERS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by selling dollars, three dealers said Friday. (published 0755 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SATYAM COMPUTER\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO HIRE 1,000 COLLEGE GRADUATES BY MID-DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Satyam Computer Services Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., now operating under the Mahindra Satyam brand, will recruit around 1,000 college graduates by mid-December, a senior company executive said Friday. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ABG SHIPYARD\f28 \uc2 \f2 , BHARATI OPEN OFFERS FOR GREAT OFFSHORE START DEC. 3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rival Indian ship builders \f28 \uc2 \f2 ABG Shipyard Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharati Shipyard Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday their competing open offers for a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Great Offshore Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will open Dec. 3. (published 0813 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RELIANCE CAPITAL OFFERS TO BUY MAJORITY STAKE IN QUANT CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reliance Capital Ltd. said Friday it has proposed to buy a majority stake in Mumbai-based Quant Capital Group for an undisclosed amount to expand its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0800 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CEMENT PRICES UP IN PARTS OF INDIA ON SUPPLY CRUNCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cement prices in some parts of India have risen in the past couple of days--after having fallen in the past few months--due to a shortage of railway wagons for transporting the commodity, the president of a Mumbai-based cement dealers' association said Friday. (published 0716 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RANBAXY LAUNCHES GENERIC VALTREX IN US, SHARES RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ranbaxy Laboratories Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said it has launched a generic version of \f28 \uc2 \f2 GlaxoSmithKline\f28 \uc2 \f2 's anti-herpes medicine Valtrex in the U.S., a development expected to significantly boost its financial results. (published 0853 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =CHARTING INDIA: INDIABULLS REAL ESTATE COULD TEST INR186 SUPPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The short-term outlook for Indiabulls Real Estate is bearish and charts suggest the stock could fall to INR186--the 127.2% external retracement of the rally from the Nov. 3 low of INR201.10 to the Nov. 6 high of INR256.90. (published 0319 GMT) [ 27-11-09 0900GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62501   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020091127e5br0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
