\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits 1-yr high as dlr slides, stx rise\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2009\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar index <.DXY> drops to 14-mnth lows; euro gains\par \par \uc2 * Rise in shares raise expectations of increased cap inflows (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed to one-year highs on Wednesday buoyed by the dollar's broad-based fall and a stronger start to the stock market that could trigger more capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 By 10:35 a.m. (0505 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 46.15/16 per dollar, off a high of 46.0950, its strongest since Sept. 26, 2008 and 0.8 percent above its Monday's close of 46.48/49.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets were shut on Tuesday for a local holiday.\par \par \uc2 "Weaker dollar overseas is fuelling selling, it is a sell uptick story," said Ashtosh Raina, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar slid to its weakest level in 14 months against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, under pressure from expectations of continued low U.S. interest rates and investor bets on commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [USD/]\par \par \uc2 Indian shares rose <.BSESN> 1 percent early, tracking mostly firmer Asian markets, but gains are expected to be limited by concern the market may have moved ahead of valuations. [.BO]\par \par \uc2 Foreign fund investments into local shares are key factor determining the direction for the rupee. Foreigners have bought a net $12.8 billion worth of shares this year, almost reversing net outflows of more than $13 billion in 2008.\par \par \uc2 At the day's high, the rupee has gained 13.3 percent from its record low of 52.2 hit in early March and is up 5.7 percent in 2009.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts <PNDF> were quoting at 46.03/13, stronger than the onshore spot rate, suggesting a bullish outlook for the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee is mostly likely to breach the 46/dollar mark, if the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Raina said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has previously said it buys or sells dollars in the spot market to prevent volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said they would watch out for any RBI action to limit the sharp rise in the rupee.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $181 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, when the rupee had risen to a two-month high, its bulletin showed on Monday. [ID:nBOM308873]\par \par \uc2 "Given the state of USD sentiment, it may just be a matter of time before targets such as 42 appear on the horizon," Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 , said in a Wednesday note.\par \par \uc2 "The modest amounts reported for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from May to August indicate strongly that the range-bound price action on the rupee at a time of sizeable gains for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not due to large scale \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  USD purchases. We would be surprised if the data for October aren't more eye-catching." (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Jarshad Kakkrakandy)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNI|RBN|ABN|M|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091017e5ae0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
