\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank sold net $55 mln in July  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2009\par 15:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $55 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July after buying more than $1 billion in the previous month, its bulletin showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 bought $570 million and sold $625 million in July, taking its net sales to $6.12 billion in the first seven months of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> touched a two-month low of 49.47 on July 13, but recouped losses to end the month flat mainly because of equity-linked capital inflows. Foreigners bought $2.4 billion worth of local equities in July.\par \par \uc2 In March, when the rupee fell to a record low of 52.20 per dollar, the RBI had sold $3.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves <INFXR=ECI> rose to $277.649 billion on Sept. 4 from $276.362 billion a week earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its weekly statistical supplement on Friday. (Reporting by Anurag Joshi; Editing by John Mair)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|SNI|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090911e59b0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
