\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank says sold $1.44 billion in May\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2009\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 10 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a net $1.44 billion in May, even though the rupee rose more than six percent on the government's strong re-election and a surging sharemarket, the bank's monthly bulletin showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's dollar sales in May were 42 percent below April's $2.48 billion, and were likely to have been concentrated in the first half of the month, when the rupee was trading between 50 and 49 per dollar\par \par \uc2 On May 16, the Congress-led coalition won national elections by a huge margin, sparking a rally in equity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The rupee rose more than 3 percent on the result.\par \par \uc2 The May \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net sales in 2009 to $7.11 billion. In March, when the rupee fell to record low of 52.20 per dollar, the RBI sold $3.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves <INFXR=ECI> were at $264.584 billion on July 3, from a peak of $316 billion in May 2008. (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by John Mair)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090710e57a0014j\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\l